<newsitem itemid="187200" id="root" date="1996-11-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Xenova Q3 loss widens on higher expenses.</title>
<headline>Xenova Q3 loss widens on higher expenses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (in million stg, unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr loss (pence)	 0.15		   vs 0.15 loss</p>
<p> Oper loss		  2.1		    vs 1.7 loss</p>
<p> Net loss		   1.9		    vs 1.5 loss</p>
<p> Revenue		    0.3		    vs 0.4</p>
<p>			  Nine months to Sept 30</p>
<p> Shr loss (pence)	 0.40		   vs 0.65 loss</p>
<p> Oper loss		  5.6		    vs 7.1 loss</p>
<p> Net loss		   5.1		    vs 6.6 loss</p>
<p> Revenue		    1.1		    vs 1.1</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said operating expenses increased in current Q3 to 2.4 million stg from 2.1 million due to more investment in drug development, as well as acquisition and financing activities.</p>
<p>Xenova Group Plc is a UK-based biotech company listed on Nasdaq in the U.S. The company also plans to list its shares on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
